{"t": 1794112391.0072913, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "files": [{"content": "def deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the standard response headers for a deprecated API endpoint.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "path": "api/headers.py"}], "message": "feat(api): add deprecation headers for v1 endpoints\n\nImplements api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date) per the API\nguidelines (Deprecation section).\n\nRefs ENG-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794112393.4885466, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n- Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` for v1 endpoints.\n- Returns the three headers required by the API guidelines (Deprecation section):\n  - `Deprecation: true`\n  - `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` (the sunset date passed in)\n  - `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nCloses ENG-91", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints (ENG-91)"}, "ok": true}
